Code review identified non-conventional loop variable naming in benchmark helper functions. The variable `j` was used as a primary loop counter where `i` is the Go community standard.

## Changes

- Renamed loop variable `j` → `i` in `createDeployments()` helper
- Renamed loop variable `j` → `i` in `createDaemonSets()` helper

```go
// Before
for j := range count {
    name := fmt.Sprintf("test-deployment-%d", j)
    // ...
}

// After
for i := range count {
    name := fmt.Sprintf("test-deployment-%d", i)
    // ...
}
```

Reserve `j` for nested loops per Go conventions.

